# Source files are always diffed as text.
#
# A single NUL byte otherwise makes Git classify a file as binary: the diff collapses to
# "Bin 0 -> N bytes" and the content becomes invisible to review, on the command line and on
# GitHub. That is a review and supply-chain problem, not a display preference — a security test
# suite that cannot be read cannot be approved. `diff` forces textual diffs regardless of content.
#
# `test/human-publish-script.test.js` asserts two things about this file: that no tracked source
# actually contains a NUL byte, and that every non-binary tracked extension appears here. Adding a
# new source type to the repository without adding it below is a test failure, not a silent gap.
*.js       diff
*.mjs      diff
*.cjs      diff
*.ts       diff
*.tsx      diff
*.jsx      diff
*.json     diff
*.jsonc    diff
*.md       diff
*.sh       diff
*.yml      diff
*.yaml     diff
*.html     diff
*.css      diff
*.py       diff
*.txt      diff
*.toml     diff
*.example  diff
